  "verbalization": "Cerliponase Alfa is associated with Neuronal Ceroid Lipofuscinosis (NCL), a rare neurodegenerative disorder, through a chain of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that NCL is linked to two key proteins, Mfn1 and Cln6, both of which are associated with the disease. This implies that Cerliponase Alfa may exert its therapeutic effect by targeting these molecular pathways, potentially modulating the progression of NCL. The integration of these associations highlights a possible mechanism by which Cerliponase Alfa could repurpose its use in treating NCL, leveraging its known role in neuronal function and its interaction with critical cellular components. The evidence supports a role for Cerliponase Alfa in influencing the pathophysiology of NCL through its interaction with Mfn1 and Cln6, suggesting a potential therapeutic benefit in this condition.",
